# Who draws into the top-right corner of the screen?
#
# Every text glyph goes through DrawGlyph ($2701), which reads the cursor from
# wTextCursorX/Y ($d732/$d733) rather than taking coordinates — so one
# conditional breakpoint catches all of them regardless of which helper or bank
# issued the draw. Filter to row 0, column >= $10, i.e. the right-hand end of
# the tab row, where EzgbTabBanner's marker gets clobbered a moment after it
# is drawn.
#
# The banner's own glyphs also match this filter; tell them apart by the
# backtrace (ours has EzgbTabBanner in it), not by the hit order.
breakpoint $2701 if ([$d733] == 0) && ([$d732] >= $10)
continue
